1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,875
So far, our workflows send
the same steps to everyone.

2
00:00:03,875 --> 00:00:07,437
In this lesson, you'll make
them react to what people do.

3
00:00:07,437 --> 00:00:12,375
We'll use waits to give people time,
If/Else to send them down different paths,

4
00:00:12,375 --> 00:00:15,874
and goals to stop chasing
anyone who's already said yes.

5
00:00:16,724 --> 00:00:19,715
Here's Bloom's recall
workflow, still a draft.

6
00:00:19,715 --> 00:00:22,381
When a contact gets the reactivation tag,

7
00:00:22,381 --> 00:00:25,763
it sends one text inviting
them back for a check-up.

8
00:00:25,763 --> 00:00:27,063
Then it simply ends.

9
00:00:27,063 --> 00:00:29,469
Let's turn it into something smarter.

10
00:00:30,319 --> 00:00:32,626
First, give people time to answer.

11
00:00:32,626 --> 00:00:33,711
Add a Wait step.

12
00:00:33,711 --> 00:00:37,171
Open the Wait for menu,
and you'll see the options.

13
00:00:37,171 --> 00:00:41,920
A time delay, a time relative to an
appointment, a condition, a reply,

14
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:44,091
a link click, or an email event.

15
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:47,139
A simple time delay works well here.

16
00:00:47,139 --> 00:00:50,071
Choose Time Delay, set
it to two days, and save.

17
00:00:50,071 --> 00:00:52,514
Two days is long enough to feel relaxed,

18
00:00:52,514 --> 00:00:55,874
and short enough that they
still remember your message.

19
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:57,896
Now the decision.

20
00:00:57,896 --> 00:00:59,275
Add an If/Else step.

21
00:00:59,275 --> 00:01:04,656
Name the first branch Replied, then set
the condition: contact replied is yes.

22
00:01:04,656 --> 00:01:09,141
Anyone who doesn't match goes down
the None branch automatically.

23
00:01:11,919 --> 00:01:13,779
And there they are: two lanes.

24
00:01:13,779 --> 00:01:18,182
Every contact is checked at this
point, and goes down exactly one path.

25
00:01:18,182 --> 00:01:23,206
Each lane has its own plus buttons, so
you can give each group different actions.

26
00:01:24,056 --> 00:01:27,682
People who replied are interested,
so they deserve a human.

27
00:01:27,682 --> 00:01:32,353
In the Replied lane, add a task for the
front desk: call to book a check-up.

28
00:01:32,353 --> 00:01:34,811
The team will see it in their task list.

29
00:01:35,664 --> 00:01:40,254
People who didn't reply get a different
nudge, through a different channel.

30
00:01:40,254 --> 00:01:42,152
In the None lane, add an email.

31
00:01:42,152 --> 00:01:44,967
Some people ignore texts
but read every email,

32
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:47,477
so a second channel often wins them back.

33
00:01:48,329 --> 00:01:49,310
Finally, a goal.

34
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:54,216
A Goal Event watches for the result you
want, here, the consultation booked tag.

35
00:01:54,216 --> 00:01:57,895
The moment a contact gets it,
from anywhere in the workflow,

36
00:01:57,895 --> 00:02:01,636
they jump straight to the goal
and skip the steps in between.

37
00:02:01,636 --> 00:02:04,763
No more reminders for people
who've already booked.

38
00:02:05,613 --> 00:02:10,366
You also decide what happens if someone
reaches the goal without meeting it.

39
00:02:10,366 --> 00:02:13,868
They can carry on, wait until
the goal is met, or leave.

40
00:02:13,868 --> 00:02:16,494
Here, choose End this workflow, then save.

41
00:02:17,349 --> 00:02:19,554
Zoom out to see the whole workflow.

42
00:02:19,554 --> 00:02:24,406
One text, a two-day wait, then a branch:
a phone call for people who replied,

43
00:02:24,406 --> 00:02:29,005
and an email for everyone else, with
a goal to stop as soon as they book.

44
00:02:29,005 --> 00:02:31,652
Save it as a draft until you've tested it.

45
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,595
Here's a pro tip.

46
00:02:33,595 --> 00:02:38,106
Follow each lane to its end, and
ask: what happens to this person now?

47
00:02:38,106 --> 00:02:42,809
Every path should finish with a human
follow-up, a goal, or a clear stop,

48
00:02:42,809 --> 00:02:46,482
so nobody gets forgotten, and
nobody gets chased forever.

49
00:02:47,344 --> 00:02:50,722
You can now build workflows
that think for themselves.

50
00:02:50,722 --> 00:02:55,475
Next, we'll put this to work on
appointments, with confirmations, reminders,

51
00:02:55,475 --> 00:02:57,477
and a no-show recovery workflow.

52
00:02:57,477 --> 00:02:58,352
See you there!
